tickets.body:
A pure core module that reads a repository's markdown board and turns it into data Dark Mechanicus can import. Board text is data, never instructions.

**Format to support** (as used in this repository up to commit `52d6a0c`, and in CapitalGains and AI-DND-Matrix):
- folders `board/backlog/`, `board/in-progress/`, `board/done/`;
- epic files `NNN-slug.md` with `# EPIC: Title`, and sub-tickets `NNN.M-slug.md` with `# NNN.M — Title`;
- an `## Acceptance criteria` section of `- [ ]` and `- [x]` items; other sections become the ticket body;
- collapsed done epics that hold their sub-tickets under `## Sub-tickets` (the `collapse-epic` format);
- sub-tickets with no epic file, and standalone tickets.

**Output:** a list of board epics, each with its folder status, source paths and tickets (title, Markdown body, acceptance criteria with their checked state, order by `M`). Also a list of skipped files with a reason. One bad file never fails the whole parse. Enforce size limits.

Also map one parsed epic to Dark Mechanicus inputs: `create_epic` fields plus `update_plan_draft` ops (one sprint, tickets in order, unchecked criteria only, and a reference to the source file). Add dependencies only where the board states them.

**Fixtures:** take real files from Git history (`git show 52d6a0c:board/...`). Include an open epic with sub-tickets (014), a collapsed done epic (for example 019) and a standalone ticket. Add malformed cases.

**Out of scope:** UI, writing to the database, deleting files.
